WEBVTT

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.140
Hey, stray mutt!

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.190
Respond if you can hear my voice.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:36.450
Tch!

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.580
You can still nod your head
even if you cannot speak.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.370
I am going to ask you a question.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.400
Do you want to live?

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.900
If you want to live...

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:56.670
...take this rice ball.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.560
Oh, dear! Sorry about that.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.040
It slipped right out of my hand.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.180
You would choose survival
over pride and self-respect?

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.680
You truly are a starved stray.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.760
You will die before long
if I leave you here.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.700
You have nowhere do go, now do you?

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:45.200
Come with us. I am willing to
throw you some scraps.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:46.660
Shut up...!

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:48.390
Don't make a fool of me!

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:56.800
I've found something most amusing.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:01.540
This should keep me entertained
even after my arrival in Kyoto.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.080
You're a disgrace!

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:39.840
Are you so desperate to live
that you would degrade yourself?

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:43.610
I cannot bear to face
your belated father...

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.620
Who cares about my dead dad?!

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:50.350
Who cares if it's disgraceful?!
You can't live if you don't eat!

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.430
What's so great about samurai?!

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:54.600
Samurai...

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.980
To hell with samurai!

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:01.760
Ah, you came to? What a relief!

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:04.760
You shouldn't get up yet.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:09.160
I don't know what happened to you,
but you're covered in bruises.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.890
If it ain't a samurai!

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:14.830
Wh-what do you want?

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:30.540
G-give it back.

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:32.540
Shuddup!

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:35.230
Dang, he's got nothin'.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.690
Y-you cowards!

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:42.980
Kid, this is what you get for ridiculing
national loyalist warriors!

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:44.530
Let that be a lesson to you!

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:52.040
Damn it! National loyalists my butt!

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.250
W-wait...

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:00.690
Where am I?

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.100
The Roshigumi's lodgings.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:05.450
Not that you'd know where that is, huh?

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:09.450
It's in Mibu Village, located at the
southern end of the capital.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.680
The capital? This is Kyoto?

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.430
Yep! Now then, what's your name?

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:16.890
I'm Heisuke Toudou.

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:19.600
Huh? Oh...

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:23.210
I'm Ibuki... Ryunosuke Ibuki.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.110
That right? Well it's
a pleasure, Ryunosuke!

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:28.820
You're welcome to call me Heisuke.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.970
I'd say we're probably
around the same age.

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:32.950
Heisuke...

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.870
I don't know if you're hungry or not,

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:37.960
but you won't recover if you don't eat.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.110
I'll go fetch some grub for you.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:50.240
Protect the Emperor?

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.180
What is the meaning of this, Kondou-san?

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:53.240
I don't know.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:58.850
At any rate, we won't know
until we speak with Kiyokawa-dono.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:04.800
DAWN OF THE DIVINE WARRIORS

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:07.280
Pardon me.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:13.810
Hey! I see you've regained consciousness.
That's great!

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:17.830
Toudou-kun asked me
to bring some food to you.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.310
I received some rice porridge
from the master of this manor.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:22.940
Oh, you shouldn't strain yourself!

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:27.350
You were terribly wounded.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:29.550
You need to take it easy.

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:32.640
I'm sorry...

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:41.690
Ah, my bad!

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:53.820
There...

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:07.340
You will die before long
if I leave you here.

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:09.240
You have nowhere do go, now do you?

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:13.720
Come with us.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:16.100
I am willing to throw you some scraps.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:19.720
Come to think of it, the man back then...

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:24.480
Huh? What're you dressed up for?

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:26.380
Thanks for looking after me.

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:28.190
H-h-hold your horses!

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:29.730
Where do you think you're going?

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.200
I appreciate all you have done for me,

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.450
but I cannot impose upon you forever.

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:36.390
I'm leaving.

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:40.540
Leaving? I-I-I said to wait!

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:43.980
Heisuke, who is that?

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:49.210
Sano-san! Shinpatsu!

00:07:56.890 --> 00:07:58.560
Hey, hold up!

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:00.850
Hey, what are you doing?! Let go of me!

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:02.670
Who, pray tell, are you?

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:04.940
He's that guy Serizawa-san picked up
on the way to the capital.

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:05.770
Hey!
He's that guy Serizawa-san picked up
on the way to the capital.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:06.690
He's that guy Serizawa-san picked up
on the way to the capital.

00:08:06.690 --> 00:08:10.610
Now that he's finally doing better,
he says he's going to leave.

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:11.360
Hey!

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:15.430
I see. So that explains
why I recognized your face.

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:17.910
How long are you going
to hold onto my collar?!

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:19.490
Let go already!

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:22.450
It's great that you're feelin' better,

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:25.080
but I don't approve of your leavin'

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:27.600
without thanking your benefactors first.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:30.440
I never asked for anyone's help.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:32.090
Why you...!

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:35.970
Ow! What was that for?!

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:38.030
Regardless of whether or
not you asked for help,

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:40.980
who do you have to thank for bein' here?!

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:44.390
You owe us for the hospitality
we've shown you!

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:47.460
What's your name?

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:50.820
I already introduced myself to him.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:52.210
Ask him for my name.

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:56.080
You've got guts!

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:58.970
It looks like one blow
to the noggin' wasn't enough.

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:02.450
Eh? Yikes, don't hit me
over every little thing!

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:05.480
I'm Ibuki. Ryunosuke Ibuki.

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:08.750
You shoulda been a good boy
and said that to begin with.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.210
I wouldn't argue with Sano if I were you.

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:13.240
He don't hold back none
when it comes to dudes.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:15.510
If you want to know someone's name,

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:17.870
isn't it only polite to introduce yourself first?

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:21.180
Oh? Now you're trying to reason with me?

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:23.480
But you've got a point.

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:27.830
My bad. I'm Sanosuke Harada. And he's...

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:29.880
I'm Shinpachi Nagakura.

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:33.430
And who am I supposed to go thank?

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:38.030
Hey, now! Were you planning to
thank him looking like that?

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:41.390
First you gotta wash your face
and straighten yourself up.

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:45.140
The well is over there.
Want me to go with you?

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:47.960
I'm not a kid! I can go by myself.

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:57.970
Move it. You're in the way.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:02.530
What was that for?!

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:05.290
What?

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:09.670
It's your fault for spacing out
while standing there.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:13.290
This well doesn't belong
to you and you alone.

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:15.860
I was washing my face.

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:17.860
You could have waited for me to finish.

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:22.550
I see no reason for me to be polite
and wait on you.

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:24.200
Excuse me?

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:27.580
What? If it bugs you all that badly...

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:32.820
...why don't we settle
the matter with these?

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:33.720
Eh?

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:36.420
Okita-kun!

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:39.820
Why don't you let it drop?

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:44.760
Hijikata-kun will yell up a storm
if you get too rowdy.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:48.980
Rowdy? What a thing to say, Sannan-san.

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:52.350
He's the one who started it.

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:55.480
And you're the one who set him up.

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:59.680
I do believe you are the one
Serizawa-san rescued, are you not?

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:02.720
Have you recovered from your injuries?

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:06.990
Yeah... Anyway, where is that
Serizawa guy right now?

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:09.790
Serizawa-san is currently out.

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:12.690
I believe he will come back tonight.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.500
He's out, huh?

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:16.750
What do you need with Serizawa-san?

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:21.800
I was told to thank him
for saving me before I go.

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:23.690
Wait a sec!

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:27.350
You aren't going to thank Kondou-san?

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:29.100
Kondou-san?

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:33.270
He's the highest-ranking person
in the Roshigumi.

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:36.690
Kondou-san, do you have a moment?

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:40.610
Sannan-kun? That's fine, come on in.

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:45.280
Are you all better?

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.970
I heard that I didn't starve to death

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:53.400
because you spoke on my behalf.

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:56.900
I figured I should thank
you before I left...

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:00.420
No, I didn't do anything
to deserve your gratitude!

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:03.910
But do you know where you'll go
once you leave?

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:05.930
Well...

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:08.100
How about it? Why don't you
stay here for a while?

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:11.610
Kondou-san, I understand how you feel,

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:13.870
but we just arrived in Kyoto ourselves.

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:16.670
We are currently dependent on
the good graces of Yagi-san,

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:18.670
the owner of this manor.

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:22.320
We cannot afford to impose
another person on him.

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:23.490
But-

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:24.800
It's just as he said.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.950
I have no intention of
inconveniencing you any further.

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:32.540
Then why don't you at least
have dinner with us before you go?

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:34.250
Goodness.

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:37.570
It would seem you have forgotten why

00:12:37.570 --> 00:12:39.440
the Shieikan suffered financially.

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:43.920
Eh?! Yeah, but, uh...

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:47.240
But that is part of what makes you
who you are, Kondou-san.

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:50.010
You bastard!

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:52.710
Do you realize whom you are speaking to?!

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:56.710
How dare you take that tone with me?!

00:12:57.020 --> 00:12:58.310
Who was that?

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:00.770
That was Serizawa-san's voice.

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:07.850
Care to repeat that, Hijikata?

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:13.310
You bastard!

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:16.690
What did you say?

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:18.920
I'll say it as many times as it takes.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:21.190
We're new in Kyoto,

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:23.810
so keep your playing around in the

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:25.580
red-light district within reason.

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:28.570
You aren't the only ones
who have to stay here.

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:32.450
Hijikata-kun, how dare you speak
that way to Serizawa-sensei!

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:34.960
I see...

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:38.770
And here we were out and about

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:41.960
laying the groundwork
for future campaigns.

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:46.240
You call that playing in
the red-light district?

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:48.530
Out laying the groundwork, eh?

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:53.220
I'd love to hear what
type of "groundwork"

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:55.220
you did in Shimabara.

00:13:57.250 --> 00:14:00.480
I don't care if you're
from the Mito Tenguto.

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:03.480
If you're going to throw your status
as samurai in our faces,

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:07.240
don't do anything to give
us reason to complain.

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:09.070
Bastard!

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:15.260
Why didn't you dodge?

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:18.600
Did you assume that I was going to stop?

00:14:19.390 --> 00:14:21.240
I wasn't going to dodge regardless

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:23.090
of whether you stopped or not.

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:26.400
I didn't say anything wrong!

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:36.420
It would hardly inconvenience

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:40.560
us if we were to stop working together.

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:43.020
If you don't like my methods,

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:45.360
you're free to return to
Edo whenever you like.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:46.750
Let's go, Niimi!

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:47.590
P-please wait for me, Serizawa-sensei!

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:48.420
Serizawa-sama!
P-please wait for me, Serizawa-sensei!

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:49.720
Serizawa-san!
P-please wait for me, Serizawa-sensei!

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:55.350
Are you all right, Hijikata-kun?

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:56.750
Sannan-san?

00:14:57.220 --> 00:14:59.100
What? Everyone's here?

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:01.300
We heard Serizawa-san's voice

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:03.750
and thought that there was trouble again.

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:06.110
Whether there is trouble or not,

00:15:06.110 --> 00:15:10.650
that man will clash with others
simply by being alive.

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:12.730
Although I'm sure that is true,

00:15:12.730 --> 00:15:15.390
you must improve at
shrugging off his antics.

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:18.240
He'll have to die and be reborn

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:20.020
at least once for that to happen.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.520
Who are you?

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:29.410
You aren't a guest of
Yagi-san's, are you?

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:31.780
I'm...

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:34.720
It's the guy who collapsed
on his way here.

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:37.240
He said he wanted to thank Serizawa-san

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:38.730
and has been waiting for his return.

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:40.790
Makes sense.

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:43.050
Hey, Ryunosuke.

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:45.690
It looks like Serizawa-san's
had a lot to drink.

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:48.860
Wouldn't it be best if you waited
until tomorrow to thank him?

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:50.090
Yep, yep!

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:52.800
Serizawa-san can't hold
his alcohol worth squat.

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:54.450
But...t

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:58.080
Okay, for now let's go back
inside and have dinner!

00:15:58.410 --> 00:15:59.560
Sounds good.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:01.060
Uh, no-

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:02.410
C'mon! It's mealtime! Food!

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:03.290
Eh?!
C'mon! It's mealtime! Food!

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:21.820
Sheesh, how could they say

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:23.820
Serizawa-san can't hold down his alcohol?

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:25.940
You're pretty bad yourselves.

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:30.960
I should get this over
with before they wake up.

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:37.350
Oh, my! Aren't you...?

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.620
I'm here to see Serizawa.

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:42.370
Is he up yet?

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:45.540
Yes, the master is in his chambers.

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:47.110
I shall lead the way.

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:52.770
After resembling a filthy cowl,

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:54.740
your face looks halfway decent now!

00:16:56.710 --> 00:16:59.480
Thanks to you, I'm stuck
living for a while longer!

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:03.000
The idea of being indebted
to you forever pisses me off...

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:03.770
Wha-?!

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:05.180
...so I figured I'd thank you.

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:06.780
Y-you bastard!

00:17:06.780 --> 00:17:08.780
How dare you speak
that way to Serizawa-sensei?!

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:10.000
Well, I'm off!

00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:13.320
What was that just now?

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:18.660
Even a dog doesn't
forget a debt of honor.

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:20.600
You're worse than a DOG.

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:23.630
What's wrong?

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:25.630
Did I piss you off again, Stray?

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:30.290
I'm not a stray! I'm Ryunosuke Ibuki!

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:33.250
No matter what name you
claim for yourself,

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:35.410
you could not possibly be a human

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:37.790
if you cannot properly show your gratitude.

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:39.660
Then what do you want?

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:41.130
I don't have any money.

00:17:41.130 --> 00:17:45.040
There are plenty of other ways
for you to pay me back.

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:47.560
What do you want me to do?

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:50.670
Work as your servant here or something?

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:55.550
It would seem you aren't
completely ignorant of the world.

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:57.490
This is ridiculous!

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:01.310
I'm sick of being shackled down!

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:03.310
You are unbelievable...

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:06.500
You owe Serizawa-sensei
for saving your life!

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:09.210
I don't recall asking him to save me.

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:15.190
Ow!

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:16.610
What the hell?!

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:23.200
Back then I believe I asked you:

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.000
"Do you want to live?"

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:28.810
How did you answer?

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:31.320
Do you want to live?

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:33.560
If you want to live,

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:35.730
take this rice ball.

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:38.240
Th-that was...

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:40.340
Damn it!

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:43.850
So you finally remember?

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:48.650
But once I've paid you back,

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:52.110
I am hightailing it out of here!

00:18:56.040 --> 00:18:58.610
He said he'd keep you here as his dog?

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:00.740
What a horrible thing to say!

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:03.990
But I could see him saying that.

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:08.120
He's the most renowned member
of the Roshigumi,

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:11.350
but he can be hard to handle
in more ways than one.

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:14.550
Shinpachi, he treats you decent enough

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:17.510
since you're both of the Shindou Munen style.

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:20.950
That man thinks of us as
nothing more than...

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:22.140
mere insects.

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:25.700
But are you okay with this?

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:28.640
Sure. It's not like I had
somewhere to go anyway.

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:31.290
I just figured that things would work out

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:32.990
once I made it to Kyoto.

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:35.950
So you want me to use

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:39.070
my influence if I am to stay in Kyoto?

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:40.560
Right.

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:44.490
We lack the connections
needed to seek protection henceforth,

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:48.080
but everyone accompanying us is strong.

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:50.290
I am sure there are ways in

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:52.300
which we could benefit from each other.

00:19:57.230 --> 00:19:58.520
I understand.

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:02.370
Very well. It is not as
though I lack connections

00:20:02.370 --> 00:20:04.970
with the lord of Aizu, who guards Kyoto.

00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:07.740
If all goes well, you
may get to speak with

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:09.740
an influential member of the Aizu clan.

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:12.960
Is-is that true, Serizawa-dono?!

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:16.380
There is no benefit in
lying over such matters.

00:20:17.010 --> 00:20:18.380
Thank you very much!

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:21.490
Please! Please take care of it!

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:25.570
But are you sure you want to rely on
one of my connections?

00:20:26.010 --> 00:20:29.500
I imagine this must not
sit well with Hijikata.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.000
No, I don't mind.

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:48.720
What's wrong, Toshi?

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:50.770
Too excited to sleep?

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:52.410
Kondou-san...

00:20:52.410 --> 00:20:55.890
Why don't you join me if you can't sleep?

00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:00.030
Steamed buns and tea, huh?

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:01.740
Looks good.

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:04.570
Are you really sure about this?

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:07.660
Am I sure about what?

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:10.410
I'm referring to Serizawa-san.

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:12.940
Well, in all honesty,

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:15.710
I'm vexed that we had
to seek help from him.

00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:20.210
But even I realize that
he's the only person

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:21.920
we can rely on.

00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:25.060
I see...

00:21:30.570 --> 00:21:34.440
Well, right now all we
need to think about is

00:21:35.150 --> 00:21:37.250
how to earn a name for
ourselves in Kyoto.

00:21:42.590 --> 00:21:43.530
Indeed.

00:21:44.210 --> 00:21:48.050
I swear that someday I will lift you up

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:50.320
and make you Japan's greatest samurai.

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:53.340
That is why I came to the capital.

00:22:13.330 --> 00:22:16.240
Why the heck did you suddenly
kick me, Serizawa-san?!

00:22:16.580 --> 00:22:18.360
Lowly mongrel!

00:22:18.360 --> 00:22:21.480
How dare you
sleep in later than your master!

00:22:21.830 --> 00:22:24.070
But that's no reason to kick-

00:22:24.800 --> 00:22:26.490
I am heading out now.

00:22:26.800 --> 00:22:28.880
Have SAKE waiting for
me by the time I'm back.

00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:31.680
W-wait a sec!

00:22:31.680 --> 00:22:33.490
How am I supposed to pay for it?

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:35.510
Get the money from Hirama!

00:22:36.720 --> 00:22:37.900
Damn it!

00:22:37.900 --> 00:22:39.900
What a way to greet the day!

00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:45.950
Sheesh!

00:22:45.950 --> 00:22:48.250
Where the heck is a liquor store?

00:22:48.990 --> 00:22:49.990
Oh, I know!

00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:53.370
I bet Heisuke and
the guys could tell me where one is.

00:23:11.300 --> 00:23:12.280
Hey, you!

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:14.440
What are you doing over there?

00:23:18.430 --> 00:23:21.350
Is either Kondou-san or Hijikata-san in?

00:23:28.480 --> 00:23:30.900
If he wants to die, let him go die.

00:23:30.900 --> 00:23:33.110
It's not like I want to die!

00:23:33.530 --> 00:23:37.560
At the very least, you aren't
desperately fighting to live!

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:40.850
LED BY DESTINY
